-- ERROR ---------------- errors/duplicate_binder_5.march

`x` is bound twice in the same parameter list or pattern. [duplicate_binder]

7 |       Pair(x, x) -> x
                  ^

    A parameter list or a pattern binds each name once, so there is no single value this name could refer to.
    Rename one of them, or write `_` for an argument you don't use. To require two values to be equal, bind two names and compare them in a `when` guard: `(x, x2) when x == x2 -> …`.

    first bound here:

7 |       Pair(x, x) -> x
               ^
    run `march --explain duplicate_binder`


